> I've tried pudding farming before, but I always seem to kill them off
> very quickly. How is it done?

> By the way, this character has gauntlets of power--does that make a
> difference?

I've never done it before, but the goal is to create an entire level
full of puddings before you start killing any. Gauntlets of power do
make a difference, you get a + to damage from a strength bonus. You
need to take them off. You also need to have all your organic equipment
rot-proofed. It doesn't really work very well with brown puddings, much
better with blacks, but it's possible. Brown puddings are weaker, give
less appeasement to your god and leave corpses less of the time than
black puddings.

Read this for other help on how to.
http://scavenger.homeip.net/autohack/PuddingFarmingHOWTO

It recommends wielding an orcish helm, but I've read that others have
had more success wielding a key.



